cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CESAL, please cite the paper below."
title: "CESAL: Cloud–Edge Security Analytics for Log-Based Incident Detection, Classification, and Controlled Response"
abstract: >-
  CESAL is a security-aware cloud–edge framework for log-based incident detection,
  classification, and controlled response. Q-BAT, a quantized EM-AT ensemble, performs
  lightweight edge-side inference; a Mahalanobis distance-based routing policy escalates
  uncertain samples to BAT, a high-capacity cloud-side ensemble. Detected abnormal
  sequences are classified into known or unknown HDFS anomaly types by a RAG-enhanced LLM
  and mapped to predefined controlled response workflows.
type: software
license: MIT
